# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Re-arms the remembered two-handed weapon when the left hand is empty.
# A cast clears the hands: the weapon lands in the backpack and the fight goes on with
# fists until it is back (user check on the archer, 2026-10-21, and the gather loops
# before it). This reads the left hand, where Razor shows two-handed weapons, every two
# seconds. The weapon seen there is remembered by serial, so no graphic is needed:
# whatever the player armed is what goes back, and a replacement is remembered the same
# way. A word cannot live in a variable (document/scripting/razor.md part 3), so no
# label names the weapon kind: the layer does. rearm_graphic adds a backpack search for a
# fresh client or after a death, when nothing is remembered yet.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ config
#
#   config__rearm_graphic
#      Graphic of the weapon to pick out of the backpack when none is remembered, or the
#      remembered one is gone. 0 picks nothing: only a weapon once seen in hand goes back.
#      5187 is the two handed axe in document/game/item-list.md.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__rearm_graphic 0


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ wait
#
#   interval__equip_retry
#      How often the hand is read. A refused equip, after a disarm for example, waits
#      this long before the next try.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! interval__equip_retry 2000


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ timer
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
timer__equip interval__equip_retry


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ state
#
#   var__my_weapon
#      The remembered weapon serial, reused across Stop and Play. 0 means none yet:
#      rediscover from the hand, or from the backpack by rearm_graphic.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
if not varexist var__my_weapon
    @setvar! var__my_weapon 0
endif


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ loop
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # REARM
    #
    # Every two seconds. Arming before a cast completes interrupts the cast (wiki Combat
    # Overview), so casting, a cursor, the item queue and hiding block this. An empty
    # left hand gets the remembered weapon back out of the backpack. With none
    # remembered, or the remembered one gone from the backpack, rearm_graphic names the
    # one to pick. A weapon already in hand is remembered once by serial. The request is
    # not proof of the equip: the next check reads the hand again.
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    if timer "timer__equip" >= interval__equip_retry
        if lhandempty
            if not hidden and not queued and not casting and not targetexists
                settimer "timer__equip" 0

                if not find var__my_weapon backpack
                    @setvar! var__my_weapon 0

                    if config__rearm_graphic != 0
                        if findtype config__rearm_graphic backpack as alias__packed_weapon
                            @setvar! var__my_weapon alias__packed_weapon
                        endif
                    endif
                endif

                if find var__my_weapon backpack as alias__weapon_to_equip
                    # lift waits for the held item. The retry timer spaces the next hand check,
                    # so a refused equip after a disarm does not stall recovery.
                    lift alias__weapon_to_equip
                    drop self lefthand
                    if config__sysmsg = 1
                        sysmsg "Weapon equip requested: serial={{alias__weapon_to_equip}}. The next check reads the hand." 88
                    endif
                    wait wait__short
                elseif timer "timer__message" >= interval__message
                    overhead "[ weapon, out ]" 254
                    settimer "timer__message" 0
                endif
            endif
        elseif findlayer self lefthand as alias__equipped_weapon
            if var__my_weapon != alias__equipped_weapon
                settimer "timer__equip" 0
                @setvar! var__my_weapon alias__equipped_weapon
                if config__sysmsg = 1
                    sysmsg "Weapon remembered from the left hand: serial={{alias__equipped_weapon}}." 88
                endif
            endif
        endif
    endif
